\f1 	1	
\f2\b Search bar
\f1\b0 : The search bar is an essential component of any dictionary app. It allows users to quickly search for words and phrases by typing in a keyword.\
\
	2	
\f2\b Word list:
\f1\b0  Once a user enters a search term, the app displays a list of words that match the query. This list may include definitions, pronunciations, example sentences, and other information about each word.\
\
	3	
\f2\b Word detail 
\f1\b0 view: When a user taps on a word in the list, the app displays a detailed view of the word. This view may include additional information such as synonyms, antonyms, and usage notes.\
\
	4	
\f2\b Favorites:
\f1\b0  Many dictionary apps allow users to save words to a list of favorites for quick access later. This feature is usually accessed through a separate screen or menu.\
\
	5	
\f2\b Settings: 
\f1\b0 The app may include a settings screen where users can customize the app's behavior, such as setting the default language, font size, or other preferences.\
\
	6	
\f2\b Feedback:
\f1\b0  Some dictionary apps include a feedback mechanism where users can report errors or suggest new words or features.\
\
	7	
\f2\b History: 
\f1\b0 The app may keep a history of the user's search terms and activity, which can be accessed through a separate screen or menu.\
\
	8	
\f2\b Audio
\f1\b0 : Many dictionary apps offer audio pronunciation for words, which can be accessed through a speaker icon on the word detail view.\
